NAME
       seq - print a sequence of numbers

SYNOPSIS
       seq [-s sep] [-w] [start [step]] stop

DESCRIPTION
       Prints numbers from START to STOP, one per line. START defaults
       to 1 and STEP to 1.

OPTIONS
       -s S   separate numbers with S instead of a newline
       -w     pad with leading zeroes so every number is the same width

EXAMPLES
       seq 5
       seq -s, 0 2 10

SEE ALSO
       xargs(1), csh(1)
